              "**Colon ( : )** comes after a complete sentence and introduces a list, an explanation or a quotation. Example: *Malvolio wanted one thing: power.*",
              "**Dash ( — )** adds emphasis, an interruption or an afterthought. Example: *Olivia marries Cesario — or so she thinks.* A pair of dashes works like brackets.",
