        "deeper": {
          "q": "Some questions cannot be answered with a fair test — for example, \"Do people who live near the sea live longer?\" Why is a fair test impossible here, and how could scientists still investigate the question?",
          "zh": "有些问题无法用公平测试来回答，例如\"住在海边的人寿命更长吗？\"为什么这里不可能做公平测试？科学家还能怎样研究这个问题？",
          "hint": "Could you choose where people live and keep everything else the same? Think about pattern seeking: collecting lots of data and comparing groups.",
          "hintZh": "提示：你能决定别人住在哪里，并让其他条件都一样吗？想一想\"寻找规律（pattern seeking）\"：收集大量数据并比较不同人群。",
          "model": "A fair test is impossible because scientists cannot (and should not) decide where people live, and they cannot keep all the other variables the same: people who live near the sea may have different incomes, diets, jobs, exercise habits and access to health care, and any of these could affect how long they live. Instead, scientists could use pattern seeking: collect data on thousands of people, compare the life spans of people who live near the sea with those who live inland, and use statistics to allow for other factors such as income and age. Even if they find a pattern (a correlation), it would not prove that living near the sea causes a longer life, because another variable might explain both.",
          "modelZh": "无法做公平测试，因为科学家不能（也不应该）决定人们住在哪里，也无法让其他变量保持一致：住在海边的人可能收入、饮食、工作、运动习惯和医疗条件都不同，这些都会影响寿命。科学家可以改用\"寻找规律\"的方法：收集成千上万人的数据，比较住海边和住内陆的人的寿命，并用统计方法排除收入、年龄等其他因素的影响。即使发现了规律（相关性 correlation），也不能证明住在海边\"导致\"长寿，因为可能有别的变量同时影响两者。"
        },
