          "hint": "Think about price, mining and the environment, which countries supply these elements — and recycling, repair and other elements in the same group.",
          "hintZh": "提示：考虑价格、采矿与环境、哪些国家供应这些元素——以及回收、维修和同族的其他元素。",
          "model": "If these elements run short, prices rise and devices become more expensive, and countries that do not mine them depend on the few that do, which can cause political and trade problems. Mining more of them can damage land and water, uses a lot of energy and sometimes involves unsafe working conditions. Meanwhile, millions of old phones sit in drawers or go to landfill with the elements still inside them. People could recycle e-waste to recover the metals (\"urban mining\"), design devices that last longer and can be repaired, and develop batteries that use more common elements. One example is the sodium-ion battery: sodium is in the same group as lithium, so it behaves in a similar way, but it is far more plentiful — there is a huge amount in seawater.",
          "modelZh": "如果这些元素短缺，价格会上涨，电子产品变贵；没有这些矿产的国家要依赖少数几个出产国，可能引发政治和贸易问题。扩大开采会破坏土地和水源、消耗大量能源，有时还涉及不安全的劳动条件。与此同时，数以百万计的旧手机躺在抽屉里或被扔进垃圾填埋场，里面的元素白白浪费。人们可以回收电子垃圾提取金属（\"城市采矿\" urban mining），把产品设计得更耐用、可维修，并开发使用更常见元素的电池。例如钠离子电池：钠和锂在同一族，性质相似，但储量丰富得多——海水里就有大量的钠。"
