          "q": "The ocean absorbs carbon dioxide from the air. As carbon dioxide levels rise, seawater is slowly becoming less alkaline: its average surface pH has fallen from about 8.2 to about 8.1. Why might this matter for shellfish such as green-lipped mussels and pāua?",
          "zh": "海洋会吸收空气中的二氧化碳。随着二氧化碳浓度上升，海水的碱性正在慢慢减弱：表层海水的平均 pH 已从约 8.2 降到约 8.1。这对青口贝（green-lipped mussels）和鲍鱼（pāua）等贝类为什么可能很重要？",
          "hint": "Carbon dioxide forms a weak acid in water. Shells are made of calcium carbonate. What do acids do to carbonates?",
