        "example": {
          "title": "Worked example — magnification and real size",
          "titleZh": "例题：放大倍数与实际大小",
          "task": "A student views onion cells with a 10× eyepiece and a 40× objective. (a) What is the total magnification? (b) She changes to the 10× objective. What changes? (c) In a photo taken at × 400, one cell is 100 mm long. How long is the real cell?",
          "taskZh": "一名学生用 10× 目镜和 40× 物镜观察洋葱细胞。(a) 总放大倍数是多少？(b) 她换成 10× 物镜，会有什么变化？(c) 在一张放大 400 倍拍摄的照片中，一个细胞长 100 mm。这个细胞实际有多长？",
          "steps": [
            "(a) Total magnification = eyepiece × objective = 10 × 40 = × 400.",
            "(b) New magnification = 10 × 10 = × 100. She sees more cells (a wider field of view), but each looks smaller and shows less detail.",
            "(c) Real size = image size ÷ magnification = 100 mm ÷ 400 = 0.25 mm.",
            "Convert to micrometres (1 mm = 1000 µm): 0.25 mm × 1000 = 250 µm."
          ],
          "stepsZh": [
            "(a) 总放大倍数 = 目镜 × 物镜 = 10 × 40 = 400 倍。",
            "(b) 新的放大倍数 = 10 × 10 = 100 倍。她能看到更多细胞（视野更大），但每个细胞看起来更小，细节更少。",
            "(c) 实际大小 = 图像大小 ÷ 放大倍数 = 100 mm ÷ 400 = 0.25 mm。",
            "换算成微米（1 mm = 1000 µm）：0.25 mm × 1000 = 250 µm。"
          ],
          "answer": "(a) × 400. (b) × 100: more cells in view, but less detail. (c) The real cell is 0.25 mm (250 µm) long.",
          "answerZh": "(a) 400 倍。(b) 100 倍：视野里细胞更多，但细节更少。(c) 细胞实际长 0.25 mm（250 µm）。"
        },
