            "model": "Arachne is presented as a gifted but dangerously proud young woman whose arrogance leads to her downfall. Her pride is clear in her boast: “Not even Athena could weave better than I.” By comparing herself with a goddess, she shows that she believes she has no equal, and the verb “boasted” has negative connotations of showing off rather than quiet confidence. Her pride hardens when she “only laughed” at the old woman’s warning: the word “only” suggests that she does not take the warning seriously at all. Because readers know that Greek gods punish mortals who challenge them, these details build tension and prepare us for her punishment. In this way, the myth presents pride as a fatal flaw, warning its audience that talent without humility can lead to disaster.",
            "modelZh": "阿拉克涅被塑造成一个才华出众却极其骄傲的少女，她的傲慢导致了她的毁灭。她的骄傲在这句夸口中显而易见：“连雅典娜都织得不如我。”她把自己和女神相比，表明她认为自己无人能及；动词 boasted（夸口）带有炫耀的贬义色彩，而不是平静的自信。当她对老妇人的警告“只是大笑”时，她的骄傲更加顽固：only（只是）一词暗示她根本没把警告当回事。由于读者知道希腊众神会惩罚挑战他们的凡人，这些细节制造了紧张感，为她的惩罚做好铺垫。这样，神话把骄傲表现为致命的缺点，警示人们：有才华而无谦逊，可能招致灾难。",
